 OPENED mfsim.nam
 FILE TYPE:NAM6               UNIT 1002   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # MODFLOW 6 simulation name file - Sagehen, configured for the SUMMA coupler
 #   * single GWF model "SAGEHEN", DIS grid
 #   * TDIS in SECONDS, MODFLOW time step = SUMMA forcing data_step (3600 s here)
 #   * RCH package "RCHA" with READASARRAYS  (recharge supplied by SUMMA each step)
 # Built from the ex-gwf-sagehen array files in this directory.

 OPENED sagehen.tdis
 FILE TYPE:TDIS6              UNIT 1003   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Time discretisation - SECONDS, two stress periods.
 #   Period 1 is STEADY STATE: one step that equilibrates the water table against a
 #     climatological mean recharge before the coupling starts.  This is what the upstream
 #     MODFLOW 6 Sagehen example does and what the coupled model lacked (section 8.5).
 #     The coupler detects it through <MODEL>/ISS, solves it with the RCH PERIOD 1 array
 #     (NOT with SUMMA drainage), and starts the coupled loop on the first transient step.
 #     perlen is nominal for a steady-state solve; 1 s keeps it out of the way of the
 #     "MODFLOW simulation shorter than SUMMA" check.
 #   Period 2 is the TRANSIENT coupled period, and its step length must equal SUMMA's
 #     data_step (3600 s), with at least as many steps as SUMMA has data steps.
 #  perlen      nstp   tsmult

 OPENED sagehen.nam
 FILE TYPE:GWF6               UNIT 1004   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # GWF model name file for model SAGEHEN.
 # Newton-Raphson for the unconfined (convertible) layer.

 OPENED sagehen.dis
 FILE TYPE:DIS6               UNIT 1005   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Structured discretisation: 1 layer, 73 rows, 81 cols, 90 m cells.
 # IDOMAIN (idomain1.txt) = 0 where the native ibnd1.txt is 0, else 1.
 # TOP/BOTM/arrays are the native ex-gwf-sagehen text arrays (row-major, 73 x 81).

 OPENED sagehen.npf
 FILE TYPE:NPF6               UNIT 1009   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Node property flow.  ICELLTYPE 1 -> convertible (unconfined) with Newton.
 # kh1.txt / kv1.txt hold the upstream ex-gwf-sagehen values in m/DAY (0.005-0.3);
 # this model runs TIME_UNITS SECONDS, so FACTOR 1/86400 converts them to m/s.

 OPENED sagehen.sto
 FILE TYPE:STO6               UNIT 1012   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Storage - transient, convertible (water-table) storage from sy1.txt.
 # SY is the active parameter for the water-table layer; SS is kept small (1e-7) so the
 # few cells that start above land surface do not release a destabilising confined-storage
 # pulse in the first hours of the transient.

 OPENED sagehen.ic
 FILE TYPE:IC6                UNIT 1014   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Initial conditions - starting heads from strt1.txt (m).

 OPENED sagehen.oc
 FILE TYPE:OC6                UNIT 1016   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Output control - keep it light for a coupler smoke test: heads/budget every
 # 24th step (daily) plus the last step.  Bump to ALL if you need every step.

 OPENED sagehen.drn
 FILE TYPE:DRN6               UNIT 1018   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Drain at land surface - groundwater discharge / saturation excess (section 8.1).
 #
 # One drain per active cell, elevation = DIS TOP, so the aquifer cannot hold a water table above
 # the ground: once it reaches land surface the excess leaves here instead of mounding.  The
 # coupler returns this flow to SUMMA as surface runoff (role = surface_discharge).
 #
 # This is what the upstream MODFLOW 6 Sagehen example uses DRN for, alongside UZF, SFR and MVR.
 # In GSFLOW this water would be routed to the nearest downgradient stream reach by MVR; with no
 # SFR network here it goes back to SUMMA's surface runoff instead, which then routes normally.
 #
 # Conductance = K_h * cell area / 1 m, a thin seepage face; K_h is from kh1.txt (m/day) converted
 # to m/s by the same 1.157e-5 factor sagehen.npf applies.  The three CHD outlet cells are excluded,
 # since they already impose a head.

 OPENED sagehen.rcha
 FILE TYPE:RCH6               UNIT 1020   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Array-based recharge (READASARRAYS).  The SUMMA coupler overwrites the RECHARGE
 # array in memory (SAGEHEN/RCHA/RECHARGE) every time step with the regridded SUMMA
 # soil-column drainage, in m/s.  The constant below is only the pre-coupling default
 # used when running mf6 stand-alone; it is a small non-zero background rate so the
 # water table does not collapse (and diverge) over a long zero-recharge stand-alone run.

 OPENED sagehen.evta
 FILE TYPE:EVT6               UNIT 1022   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Array-based evapotranspiration (READASARRAYS) - groundwater ET (section 8.1).
 #
 # The coupler overwrites the RATE array in memory (SAGEHEN/EVTA/RATE) every step with SUMMA's
 # aquifer transpiration demand: the share of canopy transpiration its deep roots want from below
 # the soil column.  What MODFLOW actually supplies comes back through the gw_et role.
 #
 # WHY DEPTH IS LARGE, NOT rootingDepth - soilDepth.
 #
 # The rate SUMMA sends has ALREADY been reduced by scalarTranspireLimAqfr, the water-table ramp in
 # soilResist - that reduction is what tells stomatal resistance how much deep water is available,
 # so it cannot be left out on the SUMMA side.  If EVT then applied its own extinction ramp on top,
 # the same limit would be imposed twice and extraction would be short by that factor: measured on
 # this domain as exactly 0.5417, which is the cell-wise mean of the ramp.
 #
 # So EVT is configured NOT to re-limit.  SURFACE sits at the base of the SUMMA soil column, where
 # psi is measured, and DEPTH is large enough that the proportion is 1 over the whole plausible
 # water-table range.  MODFLOW still refuses what a drying cell cannot supply, which is the part
 # SUMMA genuinely cannot know.
 #
 # The residual disagreement is aggregation, not double counting: SUMMA forms one limiting factor
 # from the HRU-mean water table while the real ramp is a clipped nonlinear function of a
 # water-table distribution spanning tens of metres within a single HRU.  See the write-up.

 OPENED sagehen.chd
 FILE TYPE:CHD6               UNIT 1024   STATUS:OLD                 
 FORMAT:FORMATTED              ACCESS:SEQUENTIAL          
 ACTION:READ                

 # Constant-head cells - the three outlet cells that carry ibnd1.txt == -1,
 # held at their strt1.txt value (see chd1.txt: layer row col head).

